# qwen36-a3b-tf on a Mac: TensorFold 0.6.6 (MLX), drafts on. Its speculative
# decoding drafts with the checkpoint's own MTP layer and keeps a draft only
# where it equals the model's own greedy pick, so at temperature 0 it writes
# exactly what drafts off (qwen36-a3b-tf-nodraft) writes, faster or not.
#
# 1 FIT     MLX 4-bit, groups of 64, routers 8-bit: 20.4 GB of weights (4.7 bits
#           a weight over 34.7 B parameters, the vision tower's weights
#           included) plus the 0.5 GB MTP layer. KV as llama.cpp's.
WEIGHTS_GB=20.9
# 2 ENGINE  TensorFold at rack's pinned commit (py/engines.py), in its own venv.
ENGINE=tensorfold
# 3 ACCESS  TensorFold's checkpoint: mlx-community/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-4bit's shards
#           and the MTP layer (mtp-4bit.safetensors), which drafts look for
#           beside the weights. Pinned.
. "$RECIPE_DIR/model.env"
ARTIFACT=TensorFold/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MLX-4bit-MTP
ARTIFACT_REVISION=f84b054c5677b6e59bdb969ae61915b0983d68bb
SERVE_ARGS=(
  # 4 SHAPE   the same as llama.cpp's: a 65536-token window, 4 streams at once.
  #           rack up sets --host, --port, --name, --api-key-file, --no-update-check.
  --context 65536
  --parallel 4
  # 6 SPEED   drafts: on by default (the MTP layer, up to 4 tokens a round for
  #           this model). The switch is qwen36-a3b-tf-nodraft (--no-drafts).
)
ENV_EXTRA=()
# 8 PROOF   bench/results.jsonl, labels qwen36-a3b-tf-drafts-*
